{
  "title": "用陰影回答光",
  "title_en": "Answering Light with Shadow",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 6,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-answering-light",
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 20,
  "setting": "雲霧之上的玻璃溫室",
  "subtitle": "一則學會回話的故事",
  "subtitle_en": "A Story of Learning to Reply",
  "lead": "正午的桌上，一道陽光少了一截，卻找不到是什麼擋住了它。有一種只住在霧與蒸氣裡的冷光，看不見人、也讀不懂字，只讀得到光被擋住多久、擋了幾次。她先用格子和紀錄紙去理解，後來才學會放下熟悉的方法，用自己的影子回話。",
  "lead_en": "On a desk at noon, a band of sunlight is missing a piece, and nothing seems to be blocking it. A cold light lives only in fog and steam. It cannot see faces or read words; it reads only how long light is blocked, and how many times. She first tries to understand it with grids and notes. Only later does she set her familiar methods aside and answer with her own shadow.",
  "statement": "正午的桌上，一道陽光少了一截，卻找不到是什麼擋住了它。有一種只住在霧與蒸氣裡的冷光，看不見人、也讀不懂字，只讀得到光被擋住多久、擋了幾次。她先用格子和紀錄紙去理解，後來才學會放下熟悉的方法，用自己的影子回話。\n\n理解他者，常常要先放下自己最熟悉的說話方式。這本書裡，她的影子不是形狀，而是時間：一段長、一段短、一次停頓。最後的回答很小，落在家裡的桌上、她的手影裡，而對話還在繼續。",
  "statement_en": "On a desk at noon, a band of sunlight is missing a piece, and nothing seems to be blocking it. A cold light lives only in fog and steam. It cannot see faces or read words; it reads only how long light is blocked, and how many times. She first tries to understand it with grids and notes. Only later does she set her familiar methods aside and answer with her own shadow.\n\nUnderstanding another often begins by setting aside the way we are used to speaking. In this book her shadow is not a shape but a span of time: one long, one short, a pause. The final answer is small. It lands on a kitchen table, inside the shadow of her hand, and the conversation goes on.",
  "afterword": "理解他者，常常要先放下自己最熟悉的說話方式。這本書裡，她的影子不是形狀，而是時間：一段長、一段短、一次停頓。最後的回答很小，落在家裡的桌上、她的手影裡，而對話還在繼續。",
  "afterword_en": "Understanding another often begins by setting aside the way we are used to speaking. In this book her shadow is not a shape but a span of time: one long, one short, a pause. The final answer is small. It lands on a kitchen table, inside the shadow of her hand, and the conversation goes on.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "故事中的訊號借自自然界以光說話的方式：螢火蟲用閃光的長短與間隔辨認彼此，頭足類以皮膚上流動的明暗傳遞訊息；高山上背對太陽時，人的影子會落進下方的霧裡。光潮群與它的語法，是本書的創作。",
  "story_en": "The signals in this story borrow from the ways nature speaks in light: fireflies recognise one another by the length and spacing of their flashes, and cephalopods pass messages through moving patterns of light and dark on their skin. On a mountain with the sun behind you, your shadow can fall into the fog below. The light tide and its grammar are invented for this book.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：Sara Lewis, A Guide to Lightningbug Linguistics (2018)（https://silentsparks.com/2018/06/02/a-guide-to-lightningbug-linguistics/）；How et al., Dynamic Skin Patterns in Cephalopods, Frontiers in Physiology 8:393 (2017)（https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5474490/）；NOAA Ocean Exploration, What is bioluminescence?（https://oceanexplorer.noaa.gov/facts/bioluminescence.html）",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Sara Lewis, A Guide to Lightningbug Linguistics (2018) (https://silentsparks.com/2018/06/02/a-guide-to-lightningbug-linguistics/); How et al., Dynamic Skin Patterns in Cephalopods, Frontiers in Physiology 8:393 (2017) (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5474490/); NOAA Ocean Exploration, What is bioluminescence? (https://oceanexplorer.noaa.gov/facts/bioluminescence.html)",
  "credit": "史旺基 Swanky 企劃、視覺統籌、選片與審定。",
  "credit_en": "Concept, visual direction, image selection and editorial oversight by Swanky.",
